<root>

<!-- NOTES:

  Ambient sound scape selection is defined by several factors:
   1) the actors that are near the ambient sound scape player radius,
   2) the ground tile the actor with player is standing on. This can be used to alter soundscapes when the player enters a building,
   3) the time of day, and
   4) the weather conditions.
  
  1) Actor types that want to affect the ambience selection need to:
   1.1) Have tag AFFECTS_AMBIENCE
   1.2) Have string key value "ambience_id" that refers to one of the array ids in this file.
  
  2) The ground tile type near the player can affet the sound scape if the ground tile type has string key value "ambience_id" that refers to one of the array ids in this file.
  <array id="KEY_VALUES">
  <node 
     key.STRING.ambience_id="INDOORS"
  />
  </array>
  
  3) Current time of day needs to fall into time_of_day_range defind in one of the array nodes.
  
  4) (Not defined nor implemented yet) The weather conditions as defined by tags such as WEATHER_SUNNY, WEATHER_CLOUDY, WEATHER_RAIN_LIGHT could also have an effect on sound scape selection.


  Array id defines the ambience id. Array parameter 'radius' defines the trigger radius when the sound scapes start playing.

  Array node attributes define hints when the sound scape defined should be playing:
   time_of_day_range  Time when this ambience can be selected if the time is between given range. For full day use "00:00..24:00" or do not define the attribute at all.
   radius      Override array trigger radius for this node sound scape. This needs to be less than array 'radius'.
   required_weather_tags  List any weather tags that need to be present for this to be selected.

-->
  
  <array id="SUBURBAN" radius="600">
    <node time_of_day_range="06:00..21:00" sound_scape="sound-scapes/ambience/suburban-day.xml" />
    <node time_of_day_range="21:00..06:00" sound_scape="sound-scapes/ambience/suburban-night.xml" />
  </array>
  
  <array id="FOREST_DECIDUOUS" radius="600">
